12. Customer System
The game uses two customer types.
Story Customers
Named customers with persistent history.
They track:
	• name
	• industry
	• hosted_since
	• growth_stage
	• user_count
	• satisfaction
	• contract_history
	• milestones
	• relationship_score
	• churn_risk
Story customers can:
	• grow into major companies
	• go viral
	• request expansions
	• suffer setbacks
	• become flagship customers
Background Customers
Aggregated customer groups.
Example:
	• 142 personal websites
	• 87 small businesses
	• 26 forums
	• 9 SaaS startups
Background customers provide scale without requiring individual simulation.

13. Customer Success Story System
Customer success stories are a signature feature.
A small early customer can become a major platform over time.
Example
Year 1:
PhotoSnap Startup
Small hosting contract.
Year 5:
PhotoSnap reaches 100,000 users and requests more infrastructure.
Year 12:
PhotoSnap becomes a global platform requiring multi-region deployment.
Year 20:
PhotoSnap becomes one of the player’s largest customers.
The system should generate milestone events and preserve long-term customer history.

