27. Technical Risks
Risk: Late-Game Simulation Becomes Too Heavy
Mitigation:
Use pooled simulation at rack, datacenter, and region scale.
Risk: UI Becomes Too Complex
Mitigation:
Use layered detail. Show simple summaries first, with drill-down panels for advanced players.
Risk: Balancing Becomes Difficult
Mitigation:
Keep hardware, contracts, and customer growth data-driven.
Risk: Save Files Become Fragile
Mitigation:
Use versioned save data and migration logic.

28. Summary
Infrastructure Tycoon should be built as a scalable, data-driven simulation game using Unity and C#.
The core technical identity is:
	• detailed early-game infrastructure
	• abstracted late-game infrastructure
	• story-driven named customers
	• background customer aggregation
	• systems-based failures
	• adjustable-speed simulation
	• expandable content architecture
The technical design supports the game’s central fantasy:
Start with one PC hosting one website.
Grow into a global cloud provider powering the world’s biggest companies.

